From e56421e3c3d141c884480f2ff3422b1c085e536a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mika Tammi <mikatammi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:34:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hadrian: don't use the target's libffi for a cross compiler's
 stage0

configure's --with-ffi-includes/--with-ffi-libraries describe the
target's libffi. Hadrian also passed them to the stage0 build of the
`ghc` library, which for a cross compiler is built for the build
platform. The stage0 package then carries the target libffi's library
directory, and linking the stage1 compiler resolves the bootstrap RTS's
`-lffi` against the target's libffi.

For ELF targets the linker happens to skip the incompatible archive, but
for wasm32-wasi (with libffi-wasm) GNU gold fails with "plugin failed to
claim member ffi.o" and leaves the ffi symbols undefined.

Only pass the libffi directories when not building stage0 of a cross
compiler. Stage0 then finds the build platform's libffi in its usual
search paths, as for all other stage0 packages.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
 hadrian/src/Settings/Packages.hs | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hadrian/src/Settings/Packages.hs b/hadrian/src/Settings/Packages.hs
index 5aa287d..71307e0 100644
--- a/hadrian/src/Settings/Packages.hs
+++ b/hadrian/src/Settings/Packages.hs
@@ -158,7 +158,10 @@ packageArgs = do
           -- the Stage1 libraries, as we already know that the bootstrap
           -- compiler comes with the same versions as the one we are building.
           --
-            builder (Cabal Setup) ? cabalExtraDirs ffiIncludeDir ffiLibraryDir
+            -- The libffi directories from configure are the target's. When cross
+            -- compiling, the stage0 compiler library is built for the build
+            -- platform, where they would make the linker pick the target's libffi.
+            builder (Cabal Setup) ? orM [notStage0, expr (notM cross)] ? cabalExtraDirs ffiIncludeDir ffiLibraryDir
           , builder (Cabal Flags) ? mconcat
             [ ifM stage0
                 (andM [cross, bootCross] `cabalFlag` "internal-interpreter")
